    "difficultyReason": "Part a is direct recall of n/9 for a single-digit recurring decimal. Part b is signposted: it says to take one tenth of the part a result. Part c has no signpost, so students must transfer that tenth-of-n/9 method and then simplify 6/90 to 1/15. This is more than p27-q1, which has no reverse conversion to a fraction. It is well below p29-q6, which has many parts with mixed numbers and multi-digit recurring blocks.",
